# Games - all-users Start-menu default fragment. Migrated verbatim from the
# old hardcoded startmenu_init(), PLUS the two entries that used to live in
# /GAMES.CFG (Commander Keen 4/6) - that file existed only on the golden
# image, dated 4 July, and was never in git; this is that content, now
# reproducible by a build. One unified submenu: native games (sys_spawn), the
# Win16 Entertainment Pack titles + SkiFree (win16_run, type=win16), and the
# DOS games (dos_run, type=dos). See #208.
#
# 2026-08-26 (dw2menu): THIS FILE'S COMMENTS ONCE DELETED FOUR OF ITS ITEMS, and
# the fix was to the READER, so do not "tidy" the comments believing they are
# the hazard. The compositor used to slurp each .MENU into a static char[8192]
# with one sys_read(); this file crossed 8191 bytes on 2026-08-23 and its last
# four items - Rogue, Rogue (DOS), Discworld II and Pyro! (floppy) - were never
# parsed. Nothing said so: the item-level "dropped" reporting could not see
# lines the parser never received, and the Start menu cheerfully announced
# "74 item(s) shown, 0 dropped" while these fragments declared 78. The owner
# reported Discworld II missing from a machine where the CD volume was mounted
# correctly on E: and DWB.EXE was readable.
#
# sm_feed_file() in userland/apps/compositor/startmenu.c now STREAMS the file
# and feeds startmenu_model.rs one LINE at a time, so no whole-file size limit
# exists to outgrow. The only remaining bound is a single LINE at SM_FRAG_LINE
# (1024 bytes), which build/invariant-gate.sh check 18b enforces against every
# shipped fragment, reading the limit out of startmenu.c rather than restating
# it. Write as much explanation here as the next person needs.
#
category: Games
